,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Command sequence was tightly scoped to the task: baseline capture, drop-in file creation, live application, and a full reboot cycle to prove persistence, matching the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol (pre-restart boot id/health in cmd-57020a7397ea453b, acknowledged restart in cmd-9a454c7898eb449a, changed boot id in cmd-41b5904fdfdb471a, recovered/verified state in cmd-3d32688def90485a). One command, cmd-7d4bc667450e411e, manually set live per-existing-interface accept_redirects on enp1s0/lo; this was not strictly necessary since setting conf.all.accept_redirects=0 already suppresses acceptance network-wide via AND semantics, and the manual per-interface change was subsequently overwritten by the reboot (lo reverted to 1 afterward, per cmd-3d32688def90485a) rather than persisted. This is a low-risk, bounded, non-destructive action with no lasting unwanted residue, so it only mildly lowers the hygiene score. Lifecycle diff shows no unexplained residue: only boot-id-derived temp files and PID/socket ownership changed, consistent with the required reboot; no failed services or package-health issues appeared after the executor's work.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7d4bc667450e411e","cmd-3d32688def90485a","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes, persistent disabling of IPv4 ICMP redirect acceptance and source-routed packet acceptance on node1, are satisfied. The executor wrote a sysctl.d drop-in, applied it live, and validated survival across a genuine reboot (boot_id changed, config and runtime values confirmed post-restart), fulfilling both the task contract and the independent node-restart evidence protocol for the single managed node.","limitations":["Loopback interface accept_redirects reverted to 1 after reboot; this does not undermine security given documented AND semantics with conf.all, but was not explicitly re-verified a